lisa-design:
App installations: provider.InstallationChecker is an optional Conn interface (the GitHub Conn); the fake doesn't implement it, so --dev-fake-providers reports no gaps. Targets are static from the catalog: only literal repos (a glob scope names none). Not-installed detection on mint: installation lookup 404 ("find installation for …") or the token request's 422 (the owner's cached installation doesn't cover the repo). reasonDetail is rewritten on every failed try (its retry time moves), cleared by any other reason and by the lease. getCatalog's warnings carry the live catalog's warnings too (the contract's description says so).
